cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ADHD: Anchoring Defeat by Heterogeneous Divergence"
message: "If you use this architecture or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: drewc611
    name: "drewc611"
repository-code: "https://github.com/drewc611/Ai-adhd"
url: "https://github.com/drewc611/Ai-adhd#readme"
license: MIT
version: 0.0.1
abstract: >-
  A reasoning architecture in which N subagents reason under deliberately distorted frames in
  genuinely separate context windows, a blind critic scores them against a rubric that punishes
  fluency rather than rewarding it, eight written detectors prune mechanically, and what was pruned
  ships alongside what was kept. The library compiles briefs, enforces the isolation contract and
  scores what comes back; it never calls a model. Ships with a corpus analysis package reporting
  chance-corrected inter-rater reliability and a background language model trained from scratch on
  a document library.
keywords:
  - reasoning
  - multi-agent
  - subagent isolation
  - anchoring
  - inter-rater reliability
  - Krippendorff alpha
  - language model
  - Model Context Protocol
